
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Stationery Shop Billing System</title>

<style>
    * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        background: #eef2f7;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 30px 15px;
        color: #333;
    }

    .header {
        position: absolute;
        top: 15px;
        right: 25px;
        text-align: right;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .container {
        max-width: 850px;
        margin: 55px auto 20px;
        background: white;
        padding: 30px;
        border-radius: 15px;
        box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }

    h2 {
        text-align: center;
        color: #243b55;
    }

    .subtitle {
        text-align: center;
        color: #777;
        margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .input-section {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr auto;
        gap: 10px;
        align-items: end;
    }

    label {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 6px;
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    input {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 11px;
        border: 1px solid #ccc;
        border-radius: 7px;
    }

    input:focus {
        outline: none;
        border-color: #243b55;
    }

    button {
        padding: 11px 16px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 7px;
        background: #243b55;
        color: white;
        cursor: pointer;
        font-size: 14px;
    }

    button:hover {
        opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .add-btn {
        background: #198754;
    }

    .remove-btn {
        background: #dc3545;
        padding: 7px 10px;
    }

    .clear-btn {
        background: #dc3545;
    }

    .print-btn {
        background: #198754;
    }

    table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin-top: 25px;
    }

    th, td {
        border: 1px solid #ddd;
        padding: 12px;
        text-align: center;
    }

    th {
        background: #243b55;
        color: white;
    }

    tr:nth-child(even) {
        background: #f5f7fa;
    }

    .summary {
        background: #f5f7fa;
        padding: 20px;
        margin-top: 25px;
        border-radius: 10px;
    }

    .summary p {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
        padding-bottom: 9px;
    }

    .discount {
        color: #198754;
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .final {
        font-size: 21px;
        color: #243b55;
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .message {
        text-align: center;
        margin-top: 15px;
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .actions {
        display: flex;
        gap: 10px;
        justify-content: center;
        margin-top: 20px;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    @media(max-width: 650px) {
        .input-section {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .container {
            padding: 18px;
        }

        table {
            font-size: 12px;
        }

        th, td {
            padding: 7px;
        }
    }

    @media print {
        body {
            background: white;
            padding: 0;
        }

        .header,
        .input-section,
        .actions,
        .remove-btn,
        .subtitle {
            display: none !important;
        }

        .container {
            margin: 0;
            box-shadow: none;
        }
    }
</style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="header">
    <strong>Kanak</strong><br>
    PRN: 1193
</div>

<div class="container">

    <h2>Stationery Shop Billing System</h2>

    <p class="subtitle">
        Add products and calculate your bill with a flat 20% discount.
    </p>

    <div class="input-section">

        <div>
            <label>Product Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="product"
                   placeholder="Enter product name">
        </div>

        <div>
            <label>Price (₹)</label>
            <input type="number" id="price"
                   placeholder="Price" min="0.01" step="0.01">
        </div>

        <div>
            <label>Quantity</label>
            <input type="number" id="quantity"
                   value="1" min="1" step="1">
        </div>

        <button class="add-btn" onclick="addProduct()">
            Add Product
        </button>

    </div>

    <h3>Product List</h3>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Product</th>
                <th>Price</th>
                <th>Quantity</th>
                <th>Total</th>
                <th>Action</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody id="productList">
            <tr>
                <td colspan="5">No products added yet.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="summary">

        <h3>Bill Summary</h3>

        <p>
            <span>Total Products</span>
            <strong id="productCount">0</strong>
        </p>

        <p>
            <span>Subtotal</span>
            <strong id="subtotal">₹0.00</strong>
        </p>

        <p class="discount">
            <span>Discount (20%)</span>
            <strong id="discount">₹0.00</strong>
        </p>

        <p class="final">
            <span>Final Amount</span>
            <strong id="finalAmount">₹0.00</strong>
        </p>

        <p class="discount">
            <span>Total Savings</span>
            <strong id="savings">₹0.00</strong>
        </p>

    </div>

    <div id="message" class="message"></div>

    <div class="actions">
        <button class="print-btn" onclick="printBill()">
            Print Bill
        </button>

        <button class="clear-btn" onclick="clearBill()">
            Clear Bill
        </button>
    </div>

</div>

<script>

    let products = [];

    const DISCOUNT_RATE = 20;

    function addProduct() {

        const name = document.getElementById("product").value.trim();
        const price = Number(document.getElementById("price").value);
        const quantity = Number(document.getElementById("quantity").value);

        if (name === "") {
            showMessage("Please enter product name.", "red");
            return;
        }

        if (!Number.isFinite(price) || price <= 0) {
            showMessage("Enter a valid positive price.", "red");
            return;
        }

        if (!Number.isInteger(quantity) || quantity <= 0) {
            showMessage("Enter a valid whole quantity.", "red");
            return;
        }

        products.push({
            name: name,
            price: price,
            quantity: quantity
        });

        updateProductList();
        calculateTotal();

        document.getElementById("product").value = "";
        document.getElementById("price").value = "";
        document.getElementById("quantity").value = 1;

        showMessage("Product added successfully!", "green");
    }

    function updateProductList() {

        const tbody = document.getElementById("productList");

        tbody.innerHTML = "";

        if (products.length === 0) {
            tbody.innerHTML =
                '<tr><td colspan="5">No products added yet.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }

        products.forEach((item, index) => {

            const row = document.createElement("tr");

            const values = [
                item.name,
                "₹" + item.price.toFixed(2),
                item.quantity,
                "₹" + (item.price * item.quantity).toFixed(2)
            ];

            values.forEach(value => {
                const cell = document.createElement("td");
                cell.textContent = value;
                row.appendChild(cell);
            });

            const actionCell = document.createElement("td");
            const deleteBtn = document.createElement("button");

            deleteBtn.textContent = "Remove";
            deleteBtn.className = "remove-btn";

            deleteBtn.onclick = function() {
                removeProduct(index);
            };

            actionCell.appendChild(deleteBtn);
            row.appendChild(actionCell);

            tbody.appendChild(row);

        });
    }

    function removeProduct(index) {

        products.splice(index, 1);

        updateProductList();
        calculateTotal();

        showMessage("Product removed successfully!", "green");
    }

    function calculateTotal() {

        const subtotal = products.reduce(
            (sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.quantity, 0
        );

        const discountAmount = subtotal * DISCOUNT_RATE / 100;

        const finalAmount = subtotal - discountAmount;

        document.getElementById("productCount").textContent =
            products.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.quantity, 0);

        document.getElementById("subtotal").textContent =
            "₹" + subtotal.toFixed(2);

        document.getElementById("discount").textContent =
            "₹" + discountAmount.toFixed(2);

        document.getElementById("finalAmount").textContent =
            "₹" + finalAmount.toFixed(2);

        document.getElementById("savings").textContent =
            "₹" + discountAmount.toFixed(2);

    }

    function clearBill() {

        products = [];

        updateProductList();
        calculateTotal();

        document.getElementById("message").textContent = "";

        document.getElementById("product").value = "";
        document.getElementById("price").value = "";
        document.getElementById("quantity").value = 1;

    }

    function showMessage(text, color) {

        const message = document.getElementById("message");

        message.textContent = text;
        message.style.color = color;

    }

    function printBill() {

        if (products.length === 0) {
            showMessage("Add products before printing the bill.", "red");
            return;
        }

        window.print();

    }

</script>

</body>
</html>


. Software/Tools Required:
1.	Visual Studio Code (VS Code) 
2.	Google Chrome 
3.	HTML5 
4.	JavaScript

3. Theory:
JavaScript arrays are used to store and manage multiple values, while objects are used to store data in key-value pairs. Array methods such as push(), reduce(), and forEach() can be used to add, process, and calculate data efficiently.
In this experiment, a shopping cart is created using an array of product objects. Each object stores the product name and price. The push() method is used to add products to the cart, while reduce() is used to calculate the total amount. A discount is applied based on the total cart value. The calculated total, discount amount, and final payable amount are displayed in an order summary.


Result/Conclusion:
The experiment was successfully performed. The webpage demonstrated the use of JavaScript arrays, objects, and array methods to manage shopping cart data. The total amount was calculated and the appropriate discount was applied successfully. The final payable amount was displayed correctly in the order summary. The objectives of the experiment were achieved successfully.

